                <pb facs="1076" n="980" sameAs="frus:frus1874/pg980"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram from secretary of state, Madrid, to
                        Spanish minister, Washington, 20th November, 1873. Received at 6.45
                        p.m.]</seg></opener>
                <p>No apprehension need he entertained of difficulties arising from the presence in
                    Cuban waters of United States war-vessels.</p>
                <p>Spain is at this day respected in Cuba, and we are now sending the most
                    peremptory orders.</p>
                <p>I await with impatience your reply to my telegram of last evening proposing
                    arbitration.</p>
            </div>
